      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "# Paper Path — Rules and Level Goals\n\n**Grid:** 9×9 cells, addressed as (row, col) with 0,0 at the top-left. The outer ring is always paper wall.\n\n**Cell types:**\n- `#` paper wall (solid)\n- `.` empty\n- `S` marble start (empty, exactly 1)\n- `H` home hole (empty, exactly 1)\n\n**Rotation:**\n- **E**, **→** or the ⟳ button turns the whole board 90° clockwise.\n- **Q**, **←** or the ⟲ button turns it 90° counter-clockwise.\n- Orientation k counts clockwise quarter turns, mod 4.\n- Gravity always points down the screen. In board coordinates:\n  - k=0: +row\n  - k=1: +col\n  - k=2: −row\n  - k=3: −col\n\n**Rolling:**\n- After each turn, the marble moves one cell at a time in the gravity direction.\n- It stops when the next cell is a wall.\n- Input is locked until the marble stops.\n- The marble never leaves the grid, because the border is wall.\n- On load, k=0 and the marble rests on S, with a wall directly below S.\n\n**Winning:**\n- The marble wins the moment it enters H, whether it passes over H or stops on it.\n- Rolling halts, input locks, and the win panel shows the move count.\n\n**Moves:**\n- Each accepted turn counts +1, even if the marble cannot move.\n- **Reset (R or button):** restores k=0, puts the marble on S, sets moves to 0 and keeps the current level.\n- **Next level:** the button appears only after a win. After level 3, show \"All paths complete\" with a replay option for level 1.\n\n**Difficulty targets:** the minimum number of turns, measured by a breadth-first search over (position, k):\n\n| Level | Name | Shortest solution | Constraint |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Easy | 2 | — |\n| 2 | Medium | 3 | — |\n| 3 | Hard | 4 | At least one dead-end pocket |\n\nNo level may be solvable in fewer turns than its target.\n\n**Unverified:** the actual level layouts and their breadth-first-search checks have not been produced or run yet."
