      "output": "# Paper Path — `sfx(name)` (Web Audio, no audio files)\n\n```js\nlet _ac = null;\nfunction sfx(name) {\n  const ua = navigator.userActivation, C = window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext;\n  if (!_ac) { if (!C || (ua && !ua.hasBeenActive)) return; _ac = new C(); } const ac = _ac, t = ac.currentTime + 0.01, out = ac.createGain(); if (ac.state === 'suspended') ac.resume(); out.connect(ac.destination);\n  if (name === 'turn') {\n    const len = Math.floor(ac.sampleRate * 0.35), buf = ac.createBuffer(1, len, ac.sampleRate), d = buf.getChannelData(0);\n    for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) d[i] = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * (0.6 + 0.4 * Math.sin(i / len * 40));\n    const src = ac.createBufferSource(), f = ac.createBiquadFilter(); src.buffer = buf; f.type = 'bandpass'; f.Q.value = 0.8;\n    f.frequency.setValueAtTime(900, t); f.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(2600, t + 0.3);\n    out.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t); out.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.25, t + 0.05); out.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.35);\n    src.connect(f); f.connect(out); src.start(t); src.stop(t + 0.36);\n  } else if (name === 'rest') {\n    const o = ac.createOscillator(); o.type = 'sine'; o.frequency.setValueAtTime(190, t); o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(70, t + 0.12);\n    out.gain.setValueAtTime(0.5, t); out.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.16);\n    o.connect(out); o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.18);\n  } else if (name === 'win') {\n    [523.25, 659.25, 783.99, 1046.5].forEach((fq, i) => { const o = ac.createOscillator(), g = ac.createGain(), s = t + i * 0.06; o.type = 'triangle'; o.frequency.value = fq; g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, s); g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.18, s + 0.02); g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, s + 1.2); o.connect(g); g.connect(out); o.start(s); o.stop(s + 1.25); });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe function is 18 lines long. It has no ellipses, and every bracket is closed.\n\n## How it meets the requirements\n- **Delayed AudioContext:** At the top level, the code only declares `_ac = null` and the function. No context is created, no timers start and no listeners are added. The AudioContext is built the first time `sfx()` is called.\n  - In browsers that support `navigator.userActivation`, the call does nothing until `hasBeenActive` is true. That means the page has had a key press, click or tap.\n  - In other browsers, the code relies on the caller to call `sfx()` from a user event.\n- **`turn`:** This is 0.35 s of white noise. The noise has a slight crinkle modulation and passes through a band-pass filter that sweeps from 900 Hz to 2600 Hz, which gives the sound of paper rubbing.\n- **`rest`:** This is a soft knock: a sine tone that drops quickly from 190 Hz to 70 Hz, with a 160 ms decay.\n- **`win`:** This is a bright C-major chord (C5 E5 G5 C6). It uses triangle waves, and the notes start in a quick strum spaced 60 ms apart, then ring for about 1.2 s.\n- **No audio files:** Every sound is synthesized in code.\n\n## Where to call it (according to the Puzzle rules)\n- Call `sfx('turn')` for each accepted turn: Q/E, ←/→ or ⟲/⟳.\n  - This call happens inside the user's event handler, so it is also the call that safely creates and resumes the context.\n- Call `sfx('rest')` when the marble stops because the next cell is a wall.\n- Call `sfx('win')` when the marble enters the home hole H.\n  - If the win happens on this move, skip `rest`.\n\n## Not verified\n- I did not run this in a browser. Audible playback, how loud and natural the sounds feel, and the paper-like quality of `turn` have not been tested.\n- Behavior in browsers without `navigator.userActivation` has not been tested.\n- I have not checked how the function fits into the final three.js r128 HTML file, because that file has not been produced yet."
